## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a cross‑platform native module with real‑time data streaming, careful threading, and backpressure management, plus device capability handling.

## Key Concepts
- Cross‑platform native module design (TurboModules/JSI)
- Real‑time data streaming and threading
- Backpressure, frame dropping strategies
- Privacy, permissions, device capability variance

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal API sketch (TypeScript-like)
export type DepthFrame = { timestamp: number; data: Float32Array; width: number; height: number };
export interface DepthStreamConfig { targetFrameRate: number; width: number; height: number; }
export class DepthModule {
  static startStream(config: DepthStreamConfig): void {}
  static onFrame(callback: (frame: DepthFrame) => void): void {}
  static stopStream(): void {}
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure and guarantee frame latency across iOS/Android?
- How would you handle permission prompts and user privacy for depth data?
- What tests would you write to validate backpressure behavior on slow JS threads?

