## Why This Is Asked
Tests basic RN fundamentals: FlatList usage, performance basics, accessibility, and simple async data patterns. Keeps to beginner level while showing understanding of efficient rendering in lists.

## Key Concepts
- FlatList basics
- keyExtractor and getItemLayout
- item rendering optimization (React.memo)
- accessibility labels and roles
- pull-to-refresh pattern with onRefresh

## Code Example
```javascript
import React from 'react';
import {FlatList, View, Text, Image} from 'react-native';

const ChatList = ({ messages }) => (
  <FlatList
    data={messages}
    keyExtractor={m => m.id}
    renderItem={({ item }) => (
      <View style={{ alignSelf: item.isMine ? 'flex-end' : 'flex-start', padding: 6 }}>
        <Text accessibilityLabel={`Message from ${item.sender}`}>
          {item.text}
        </Text>
      </View>
    )}
    ItemSeparatorComponent={() => <View style={{ height: 1, backgroundColor: '#eee' }} />}
    getItemLayout={(_, index) => ({ length: 60, offset: 60 * index, index })}
    onRefresh={() => {}}
    refreshing={false}
  />
);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle dynamic item heights for very long messages?
- What test plan would you propose to validate 60fps rendering and accessibility on iOS and Android?

